Subject: [PATCH 1/2] PUBLISH-FIX-107: the learner can start - minScored 1000
 -> 300

Owner directive 2026-09-21 (David): "If you think dropping from 1000 to
300 speeds us go for it !!"

minScored is how many SCORED looks a gate needs before the learner may
even PROPOSE moving its line. The 1000 was set on 09-19 - before
PUBLISH-FIX-92 found the maturation sweep silently stalled: 6,941 judge
looks in 48 hours with ZERO outcome rows, because a settlement row was
dropped as a duplicate of the row it settled. So for the whole life of
the gate learner, nothing was ever counted toward the thousand. That
number was not cautious, it was moot.

With the grader working, 300 is reachable in days instead of weeks.

Exactly one number moved. Untouched: minCohort 100, minForward 100
looks scored AFTER the proposal, bootstrap confidence 0.9 that the
admitted looks' 15-minute return does not fall, one step per gate per
cycle, inside the gate's own fixed band, PROPOSED -> forward-tested ->
PUBLISHED, REVERTED if a published line stops holding, every move one
line in the log, DEGRADE so a failing learner never blocks the run.

test/publish-fix-107-learner-can-start.test.js (5) proves it is one
number: the other four guards, the derived environment, that the Judge's
bands and the learner's bands are the SAME bands for exactly the five
flow lines, and that the learner has no idea what REWARD_RISK_MIN,
scenarioStressedLoss or the size ladder are.

